# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for atophttpd.
#
# httpd_stop is a `volatile sig_atomic_t` set by the SIGTERM/SIGINT handler and
# polled by the acceptor loop to request a clean shutdown. This is the standard
# async-signal shutdown idiom and is safe, but TSan reports the handler write
# racing with the loop read because it cannot reason about signal delivery.
race:httpd_on_terminate
